messages_in_week:
['test: add a delay after starting the npm registry

Attempt at improving test reliability on CI', "docs: Update readme for 0.x.x

Add to Q&A section on how to configure `semantic-release` for 0.x.x development.

I couldn't find this information until I'm almost ready to publish a `commit-analyzer-zero` for this purpose.", 'feat(gitlab): provide support for gitlab based repositories. To enable the support the github based verification checks are refactord into own verificationConditions plugin. Also the plugin mechanism is modified a little so that all plugins can be called with Array notation.

The configuration for gitlab scenarios is as follows:
package.json
{
 "release": {
    "debug": false,
    "verifyConditions": "semantic-release/dist/lib/plugin-noop"
  },
  scripts: {
    "semantic-release": "semantic-release pre && npm publish"
  }
}', 'chore(package): update @semantic-release/github to version 2.2.3', 'test: limit information stored in context

Store only objects set in `beforeEach` used in `test`.
Avoid logging useless info on test failure.', 'chore(package): update fs-extra to version 5.0.0', "Merge branch 'caribou' into gitlab-support", 'fix(gitlab): improved test coverage and adapted code style according js-standard', 'chore(package): update prettier to version 1.9.2', 'Update README.md

Add missing colon']
